"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nWhen I first encountered the title, I thought it was about murdering someone remotely through meditation.  \nIt was , where one commits a murder and then coolly overcomes the crisis through meditation.  \nOf course, it might have been because of meditation that the case started.  \n\nThe last scene seems like a scene that leaves room for the next season.  \n\nFrom the beginning, it felt like a novel made with visualization in mind.  \nIt definitely feels like a US drama, and it seems like a subject matter that would be interesting even if visualized.\n"